{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion","id":980415,"title":"War of the Dragon Kings Discussion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-02T13:45:07-07:00","id":980415,"title":"War of the Dragon Kings Discussion","content":"Have to say I found the &quot;War of the Dragon Kings&quot; one of the most unique ideas, in the entire Shattered Dreams PDF.<br /> <br /> felt it deserves its own thread to discuss things, many things<br /> <br /> If it says anywhere tell me, but does it offer an explanation on why Dracid Bones never got found by Paleantolagists.<br /> <br /> Is it safe to say the Mnesis Background isnt purchasable at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-02-2016, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T14:25:43-07:00","id":980427,"title":"","content":"First of all, thanks, I'm very proud of that section. I'm proud of the whole book, but the Dragon Kings are something new and unique in the WtA universe.<br /> <br /> Regarding Drachid remains - we didn't have the word count in a book that necessarily focused on the Wars of Dragons and not every nuance of their life. My draft thoughts on this are (1) Chance, (2) Burial rituals (3) Mnesis, and (4) Wait. 2 and 3 are somewhat combined.<br /> <br /> The first - chance - recognizes that fossils are a pretty lucky thing to find surviving so many hundreds of millions of years. The fossils we've discovered have been estimated to maybe account for 1% of the number of creatures that lived through the enormity of the time period.<br /> <br /> 2 and 3 - Rites and Mnesis - the Dragon Kings had procedures for dealing with their dead, much like we do today. This may have included rituals that dissolved the body back into nothingness. The Dragon Kings possibly had Mnetic 'coffins' and 'crematoriums' that dissolved the bodies and gave them back to the Mnesis. This kind of religious dedication would be consistent with the awe and reverence the Kings held the Mnesis. Another possibility was that they entombed the bodies within the Mnesis, in grand imaginatory structures that would still be there if not for the collapse of the realm.<br /> <br /> The last - wait - ties into the previous explanations and acknowledges that even if the Dragon Kings did destroy bodies on death, they couldn't have gotten every one, with all their wars and chaos. One day fossilized Drachid remains may be found. Wouldn't that be an interesting shake-up for the world?<br /> <br /> Another idea is to take the creation of Drachid as 'born from Gaia's dreams of what could be' more literally. The Drachid survived and bred true because Gaia's dreams were intimately connected to the Mnesis. Once the Dragon Kings killed the Mnesis, the remains of Drachid simply dissolved into nothingness. Survivors continued on, as Gaia's gift of life spark triumphed over the Mnesis's gift of form, but once life escaped the body, the shell dissolved away. Much like Mnetic creations themselves.<br /> <br /> So there's a few ideas. Yes, I've spent some time thinking about it. If we ever get the chance to write an entire source book around this era, I'd expect that we'd dedicate some word count to covering these aspects of Dragon King life, and what became of the Drachid.<br /> <br /> I'm happy to discuss this, other questions about the War of Dragons, or other questions about the book in general. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T15:24:11-07:00","id":980446,"title":"","content":"Am I devaluing the setting from the book if I want to play IN the setting, not through its Fall? <br /> <br /> How central to life would the Dragon Kings be.<br /> <br /> would gains, or losses of Rank, or ROP's be relatively public ceremonys, in your opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T17:26:24-07:00","id":980490,"title":"","content":"Not devaluing it at all. We tried to give enough info that you could play in setting - though you'll have to fill in a few gaps and holes yourself. (Like figuring out which Gifts apply, and which don't.)<br /> <br /> How central Dragons Kings are depends on what kind of game you want to play. And IMO, Dragon Kings are into pomp and ceremony and reputation - rank increases would be rather public. (There's a reason we included Blazonry as one of the substituted skills!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T17:44:30-07:00","id":980499,"title":"","content":"Hmmmn one question on the Anasni, How much do you think they'd be culturally by the fact that the Triats in Balance at this period of time.think they would still have aspects or what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T19:29:16-07:00","id":980525,"title":"","content":"Hi Prince of the Night! I co-wrote War of Dragons with Bunyip, and I can't tell you how pumped I am to see you're enjoying it!<br /> <br /> I absolutely second Bunyip, too, in that it's not devaluing it AT ALL to want to play &quot;in&quot; the setting. I really want to play it myself! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Re: the centrality of Dragon Kings - good question! Personally, I tend to run very &quot;street-level&quot; games, so I wanted to make sure that the Drachid were *as* important, story-wise, as their Gaia-blessed cousins (don't try to tell the Kings that, though!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T04:54:46-07:00","id":980706,"title":"","content":"Thank you NateD<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on my question on the Anasni, think they'd have Aspects, or what?<br /> <br /> As the triats in relative balance at this point in time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:39:22-07:00","id":981169,"title":"","content":"Good question! We really didn't have enough words to give much time to the Ananasi (and they really weren't the focus of the Chapter, of course), but I DO have thoughts (extremely non-canon, untested, and not overly thought-out thoughts, that is).<br /> <br /> In short, though, I think of the Mesozoic Ananasi as a very alien, separate race to the Dragon Kings and Drachid. Without humanity to bridge the gap, the two species really didn't have much to unite them. Similarly, the Dragon Kings believed they ruled the world - by divine right, really - while the Ananasi were left to scuttle in the darkness, out of sight.<br /> <br /> If I got to write more (and who knows, maybe one day we will?), I'd have that carry over to their religion and spirituality, too. While the Drachid revered Gaia, but didn't think too much about the Triat (I *hope* that came across in the chapter?), I'd like for the Ananasi to focus a lot more on the Triat. They were the strange, exotic, mysterious occultists of the Mesozoic era, hoarding secrets that the Drachid only glimpsed.<br /> <br /> All of that is to say: yeah, I think that Aspects would definitely remain. I'd have loved to explore what exactly serving a (relatively) harmonious Triat would look like, too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T03:05:38-07:00","id":982034,"title":"","content":"Maybe it just gave them specialization when hiring themselves out as viziers, or assasins?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T14:21:43-07:00","id":986950,"title":"","content":"Is it possible these Dragon Kings could be the same as the Dragon Kings from Exalted?<br /> <br /> <br /> Colleen","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T14:45:58-07:00","id":986960,"title":"","content":"Wait a minute. Shattered Dreams takes place in the MESOZOIC ERA??? This is going to really mess up my crossover timeline. My timeline has the first Mokole being created by the Exalted-era Dragon Kings around 13,000 BC, which is a lot more recently than the Mesozoic Era. This is not good.<br /> <br /> <br /> Colleen","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T15:49:27-07:00","id":986983,"title":"","content":"If its important to your home cannon....just bend it to your will","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T15:52:06-07:00","id":986986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=986960#post986960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait a minute. Shattered Dreams takes place in the MESOZOIC ERA??? This is going to really mess up my crossover timeline. My timeline has the first Mokole being created by the Exalted-era Dragon Kings around 13,000 BC, which is a lot more recently than the Mesozoic Era. This is not good.<br /> <br /> <br /> Colleen</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> only the part with the Dragon kings takes place in the Mezoic Era.<br /> <br /> and the PDF has rich details on a lost prehistoric civilization, which while advanced in its own way never felt the need for the written word.<br /> <br /> Oh? <br /> <br /> ideas on how to involve Rokea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-13-2016, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T17:30:00-07:00","id":987012,"title":"","content":"Change the timelines to your own desires. That's the beauty of timey-wimey adventuring, house games, and non-canonical settings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Dragon King War is even easier due to taking part, largely, in undefined other-realms of dreams, time, and minds. Is any of it 'true'? Or was it all created whole-cloth five minutes ago as a memory of events that didn't happen by Wonderworkers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:34:35-07:00","id":987031,"title":"","content":"yeah in the mokole book its strongly painted as &quot;uber optional&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> oh a question?<br /> <br /> does it go against the spirit of things, for someone to claim a power for their archid form to let them to explore one of the other breeds turfs? <br /> <br /> e.g. a dino saur becoming airborn, or a pteordectyle deciding to go aquatic, or is that probaly understandable since the setting lets you &quot;Reshape&quot; your archid form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:40:18-07:00","id":987033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=981169#post981169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good question! We really didn't have enough words to give much time to the Ananasi (and they really weren't the focus of the Chapter, of course), but I DO have thoughts (extremely non-canon, untested, and not overly thought-out thoughts, that is).<br /> <br /> In short, though, I think of the Mesozoic Ananasi as a very alien, separate race to the Dragon Kings and Drachid. Without humanity to bridge the gap, the two species really didn't have much to unite them. Similarly, the Dragon Kings believed they ruled the world - by divine right, really - while the Ananasi were left to scuttle in the darkness, out of sight.<br /> <br /> If I got to write more (and who knows, maybe one day we will?), I'd have that carry over to their religion and spirituality, too. While the Drachid revered Gaia, but didn't think too much about the Triat (I *hope* that came across in the chapter?), I'd like for the Ananasi to focus a lot more on the Triat. They were the strange, exotic, mysterious occultists of the Mesozoic era, hoarding secrets that the Drachid only glimpsed.<br /> <br /> All of that is to say: yeah, I think that Aspects would definitely remain. I'd have loved to explore what exactly serving a (relatively) harmonious Triat would look like, too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I want to also say I loved the Dragon Kings Era. I do really wish for a second Shattered Dreams sort of book, too. I'd love to see the Mezoic and pre-human Shapeshifters explored. Even the possibilities of lost shapeshifters not yet known of or the proto-shifters of modern lines that may have split off from eachother (like the Nagah and Corax). <br /> <br /> I do wish that the Insect Wars had been explored more in reference to the Ananasi. It was mentioned some in their old Breedbook and seems like it would make for interesting material. A dark war of Weaver shifters and Spiders right under the Mokoles' noses. <br /> <br /> All things said, I have to hand it to you Bunyip and NateD, the Dragon Kings portion was easily my favorite part of the book. Thank you for all your hard work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:45:14-07:00","id":987040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Threadwrought</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987033#post987033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...All things said, I have to hand it to you Bunyip and NateD, the Dragon Kings portion was easily my favorite part of the book. Thank you for all your hard work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, way to make my entire day! Thanks so much, and I'm so glad you enjoyed it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: oh, and I'd love to do a more Ananasi-focussed look at the Mesozoic, too! I get the impression that I may be in the minority, but I really like the whole concept of the Insect Wars. I too think that the entire thing would be pretty much invisible to the Dragon Kings, too - quite literally beneath their notice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":2653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","user":"NateD","date":". 10-13-2016, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:51:36-07:00","id":987044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987031#post987031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah in the mokole book its strongly painted as &quot;uber optional&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> oh a question?<br /> <br /> does it go against the spirit of things, for someone to claim a power for their archid form to let them to explore one of the other breeds turfs?<br /> <br /> e.g. a dino saur becoming airborn, or a pteordectyle deciding to go aquatic, or is that probaly understandable since the setting lets you &quot;Reshape&quot; your archid form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't have any problem with that at all - the Dragon Kings are, generally speaking, the &quot;focus&quot; of this chapter, so anything to keep them in the action. Also, as you say, the idea of shaping and reshaping reality to suit them was a very strong theme for the Kings, so that absolutely fits. And personally, I love the idea of an elite squad of El-Khaatari soldiers reshaping themselves into plesiosaur-like Archid forms to go and infiltrate an underwater Alsepeaki lab. That would be sweeet!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T18:51:53-07:00","id":987045,"title":"","content":"Sadly for me I've been busy with work so reading is slow going. I'm looking forward the most to the Dragon Wars section, but I'm treating it like Mac and Cheese at dinner....best for last...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T04:13:37-07:00","id":987182,"title":"","content":"Well, I did it. I cut the last strings connecting the origins of the Changing Breeds to Exalted in my crossover timeline. I am now officially ready to accept Shattered Dreams as canon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Colleen","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T14:55:08-07:00","id":987457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987182#post987182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I did it. I cut the last strings connecting the origins of the Changing Breeds to Exalted in my crossover timeline. I am now officially ready to accept Shattered Dreams as canon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Colleen</div> </div> </div> </div>We must have written something compelling, for you to make such a big change. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T17:27:23-07:00","id":987504,"title":"","content":"You know, I'd love to learn more about the Drachid. Like if there was any trouble at first with the first three types of Dragon Kings' Drachid forms interacting (since dinosaurs, pterosaurs, and marine reptiles really were so distinct). <br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd even love to learn about the time before Drachid. When the Dragon Kings were three different races of shifters. Did these shifters have distinct identities and names for themselves? Practices? Beliefs? <br /> <br /> And then back to the Drachid. From the mention in the Chronicle dealing with Nightmaster, there were 'smooth skinned' Drachid that were the last remnants of their race after the wars. Does this imply the Drachid perhaps thrived off of the added genetics that Dragon Kings mixed into their gene pool? An extra dash of reptilian goodness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:54:49-07:00","id":987563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Threadwrought</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987504#post987504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I'd love to learn more about the Drachid. Like if there was any trouble at first with the first three types of Dragon Kings' Drachid forms interacting (since dinosaurs, pterosaurs, and marine reptiles really were so distinct).<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd even love to learn about the time before Drachid. When the Dragon Kings were three different races of shifters. Did these shifters have distinct identities and names for themselves? Practices? Beliefs?<br /> <br /> And then back to the Drachid. From the mention in the Chronicle dealing with Nightmaster, there were 'smooth skinned' Drachid that were the last remnants of their race after the wars. Does this imply the Drachid perhaps thrived off of the added genetics that Dragon Kings mixed into their gene pool? An extra dash of reptilian goodness?</div> </div> </div> </div>All great questions, Threadwrought! I'd love to write it, too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd especially love to write a bit more post-apocalyptic (or is it post-post-apocalyptic?) Drachid goodness, too. There's a huge swathe of time that we had to breeze through pretty quickly, there - in my head, I pictured whole other Drachid-only empires rising and falling during those eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T20:12:56-07:00","id":987574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987563#post987563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All great questions, Threadwrought! I'd love to write it, too! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd especially love to write a bit more post-apocalyptic (or is it post-post-apocalyptic?) Drachid goodness, too. There's a huge swathe of time that we had to breeze through pretty quickly, there - in my head, I pictured whole other Drachid-only empires rising and falling during those eras.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see it. The world was still just as large back then as it is now, and look at all the human countries, empires, city-states, and distinct cultures it has played host to in just a sliver of time geologically. <br /> <br /> Even with the challenges posed by the death of Mnesis and their possible genetic downfall, the Drachid would have had likely at least a millenia? Maybe more? <br /> <br /> Something else that regards the matter as to why Drachid evidence wouldn't have been found... I tend to like the idea, that, though born of Gaia's dreams, they were indeed physical beings with physical remains. But perhaps they emulated the way Mnesis dissolved back into itself with their rituals. Things like an open air burial would likely scatter bones and do a poor job preserving them. <br /> <br /> And who knows? The people of WoD may have a few Drachid bones without knowing. There are plenty of singular fossil bones or even limbs (a famous pair of enormous claws jumps to mind) without anyone being sure what particular dinosaurs they're from. Or, some are even put together in seemingly correct combinations, only for the error to be discovered years later. So many possibilities!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T21:04:17-07:00","id":987590,"title":"","content":"Oh a curious question on the &quot;Time travel dimension crossing&quot; idea, in the book, it has the line &quot;As good as it gets&quot; but think its ok for some last gifts from apis or grondr to remain, like cleansing the land of blights, or blessing a kin family with heightened fertility, or blessing a metis to have a healthy child?<br /> <br /> any of those could make compelling stories I think<br /> <br /> not sure what kind of gifts a Camazotz or Khara could give.<br /> <br /> On that, speaking of which, think the Dracid, are capable of forming human style vocalizations, if a Dragon king comes into modern earth with the nighmasters screwing history up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T21:59:16-07:00","id":987606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987590#post987590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh a curious question on the &quot;Time travel dimension crossing&quot; idea, in the book, it has the line &quot;As good as it gets&quot; but think its ok for some last gifts from apis or grondr to remain, like cleansing the land of blights, or blessing a kin family with heightened fertility, or blessing a metis to have a healthy child?<br /> <br /> any of those could make compelling stories I think<br /> <br /> not sure what kind of gifts a Camazotz or Khara could give.<br /> <br /> On that, speaking of which, think the Dracid, are capable of forming human style vocalizations, if a Dragon king comes into modern earth with the nighmasters screwing history up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since the original timey wimey thingy was Past Lives and specifically was the original source of Gifts for the White Howlers, Apis, Grondor, and Camazotz go for it guidelines would include nothing above level 3 and or relied on the unique structure of the Changing Breed in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T22:15:50-07:00","id":987616,"title":"","content":"Just read this section and was blown away by the sheer epic grandeur and *potential* of this setting.<br /> <br /> After sending the final draft to the printers, did you fellas ever think &quot;Gee, this has potential to be a Whole Role Playing Game Setting/Rulebook of its own, called &quot;Dreams of The Dragon kings&quot; perhaps?<br /> <br /> No, seriously; from the few illustrations and the *vividly* wonderous descriptions of Jules-Verne Pulp Science meets Edgar Rice Boroughs Martian Kingdoms Exoticism and Robert E Howard Barbaric Babylonian Decadence, this &quot;Game Line&quot; (if ever gotten off the ground) has the potential to be White Wolf's most fresh and original &quot;rip roaring pulp novel Adventure Game&quot; since &quot;Exalted&quot;<br /> <br /> Please give it some thought! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T22:31:06-07:00","id":987621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987606#post987606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Since the original timey wimey thingy was Past Lives and specifically was the original source of Gifts for the White Howlers, Apis, Grondor, and Camazotz go for it guidelines would include nothing above level 3 and or relied on the unique structure of the Changing Breed in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know all that was thinking let a gift they'd allready used linger.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T23:39:36-07:00","id":987644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987606#post987606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Since the original timey wimey thingy was Past Lives and specifically was the original source of Gifts for the White Howlers, Apis, Grondor, and Camazotz go for it guidelines would include nothing above level 3 and or relied on the unique structure of the Changing Breed in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Past Lives wasn't very timey-wimey. It was a vision quest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T23:55:58-07:00","id":987650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987590#post987590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh a curious question on the &amp;quot;Time travel dimension crossing&amp;quot; idea, in the book, it has the line &amp;quot;As good as it gets&amp;quot; but think its ok for some last gifts from apis or grondr to remain, like cleansing the land of blights, or blessing a kin family with heightened fertility, or blessing a metis to have a healthy child?<br /> <br /> any of those could make compelling stories I think<br /> <br /> not sure what kind of gifts a Camazotz or Khara could give.<br /> <br /> On that, speaking of which, think the Dracid, are capable of forming human style vocalizations, if a Dragon king comes into modern earth with the nighmasters screwing history up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just remember this particular thread is focused on the Dragon Kings, rather than the entirety of Shattered Dreams. <br /> <br /> As for the Drachid... I'm not entirely sure? They might, or be able to mimic certain portions. That being said, the typical vocalizations of at least modern reptiles and birds are often very different from apes. Perhaps they may have some capability for mimicry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T01:51:45-07:00","id":987674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987616#post987616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just read this section and was blown away by the sheer epic grandeur and *potential* of this setting.<br /> <br /> After sending the final draft to the printers, did you fellas ever think &quot;Gee, this has potential to be a Whole Role Playing Game Setting/Rulebook of its own, called &quot;Dreams of The Dragon kings&quot; perhaps?<br /> <br /> Please give it some thought! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Yes we* did. Pretty sure we were all hooked from the get go. Now we can hope and dream the various folks with more say than us 'mere' freelancers agree. And (I can only assume) they'll do that with more fan noise about how great it is... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *Not that I want to speak for everyone, of course, but certainly I** did.<br /> <br /> ** And I think it's pretty safe to say Nate and Bunyip did. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T07:36:17-07:00","id":987739,"title":"","content":"oh a few questions on the setting<br /> <br /> ideas on how things would be culinary wise?<br /> <br /> would they cook their food , is their anything amongst the plants they could use for fermentation.<br /> <br /> It says a Dragon Kings Auspice can change, is it safe to say that their should be a rite for doing so.<br /> <br /> since they dont just renunciate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-15-2016, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T13:36:47-07:00","id":987914,"title":"","content":"Food is an interesting topic. In the real world the flora of the dinosaur era was quite different to what humans evolved around. No grasses, few recognizable fruits. Lots of ferns, cycads, firs... Basically I'd run a few google searches and play up the differences. Plus meat, fish, bugs, insects and so on.<br /> <br /> To run a game set in the Age of Dreams, those alien differences would get supplemented by Mnetic feasts that taste as wonderful as the dreamer can imagine. These glamoured meals could be the equivalent of modern day booze, or harder even drugs. Each succulent bite dangerously addictive. Those who fail to eat real food often enough slowly wasting away as they continue to gorge.<br /> <br /> These dream fruits could have many other properties too - medicinal uses for example, attention focusing, mind enhancing, or strength boosting effects. All that and more.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine wastrels addicted to such stuff are generally pitied by those who are not. And due to the existence of such wonders, there's no need for cooking or fermenting the non-mnetic meat and veg.<br /> <br /> Just spitballing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:09:30-07:00","id":987930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987914#post987914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Food is an interesting topic. In the real world the flora of the dinosaur era was quite different to what humans evolved around. No grasses,</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poaceae#Evolutionary_history\" target=\"_blank\">Yes. grasses!</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> few recognizable fruits. </div> </div> </div>Specifically, they would probably all be rather tiny, with small seeds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lots of ferns, cycads, firs... Basically I'd run a few google searches and play up the differences. Plus meat, fish, bugs, insects and so on. </div> </div> </div>Horsetails of unusual size, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:29:43-07:00","id":987939,"title":"","content":"Ooh! Thanks for that link! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> /scurriesofftoread","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T17:18:50-07:00","id":988014,"title":"","content":"Have you guys considered pitching a Dragon Kings Era book to Onyx Path? Especially once copies of Shattered Dreams are up for everyone to get a look at? <br /> <br /> It's such a huge era with so much potential. Plus the chance to look at the Insect Wars, perhaps the other early shifters Rokea claim they fought in the depths, the specific varna and breed species that pterosaur, marine reptile, and dinosaur shifters had before the age of Drachid and Dragon Kings, and even the various possibilities for what the Wonder-Work was. There might even be a chance to examine how the earliest proto-Corax and Nagah first started to split away from the Mokole. <br /> <br /> And of course are the examinations of the Drachid themselves. From various empires to how their Dragon King ancestry showed in their variations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T00:41:00-07:00","id":988168,"title":"","content":"Wow, I am absolutely *floored* by all the interest and kind words here! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> And just as Nikink predicted: yes, *I* absolutely see the potential for the Dreams of the Dragon Kings to grow, too! Hopefully the fans do, as well - if so, who knows what could happen? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Interestingly, it took me a little while to fall in love with the setting, myself - but as I delved into the brief and started seeing all the Howard-esque possibilities crystallize (good call on all those influences, too - they're EXACTLY what I was going for!), I was ALL about it. It's so epic and wondrous and foreign, but all so familiar as well (if you've ever read history, that is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T00:43:14-07:00","id":988169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Threadwrought</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=988014#post988014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you guys considered pitching a Dragon Kings Era book to Onyx Path? Especially once copies of Shattered Dreams are up for everyone to get a look at?</div> </div> </div> </div>You better believe I have! We'll see what happens next pitch season, eh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T00:51:04-07:00","id":988173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987914#post987914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Food is an interesting topic. In the real world the flora of the dinosaur era was quite different to what humans evolved around. No grasses, few recognizable fruits. Lots of ferns, cycads, firs... Basically I'd run a few google searches and play up the differences. Plus meat, fish, bugs, insects and so on.<br /> <br /> To run a game set in the Age of Dreams, those alien differences would get supplemented by Mnetic feasts that taste as wonderful as the dreamer can imagine. These glamoured meals could be the equivalent of modern day booze, or harder even drugs. Each succulent bite dangerously addictive. Those who fail to eat real food often enough slowly wasting away as they continue to gorge.<br /> <br /> These dream fruits could have many other properties too - medicinal uses for example, attention focusing, mind enhancing, or strength boosting effects. All that and more.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine wastrels addicted to such stuff are generally pitied by those who are not. And due to the existence of such wonders, there's no need for cooking or fermenting the non-mnetic meat and veg.<br /> <br /> Just spitballing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Loving all of that, Nikink! I was thinking in a similar vein, actually. <br /> <br /> I'd also love to play around with the fact that plesiosaurs, pterosaurs and a lot of saurian dinosaurs were all obligate carnivores. I haven't seen too many fictional societies (or collections of societies) where the writers have treated cannibalism as anything more than &quot;look how evil these guys are!&quot;, but that could be QUITE interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T17:02:26-07:00","id":988524,"title":"","content":"So many good questions and ideas to respond to. Apologies if I've missed anyone.<br /> <br /> Caveat: These are just my unofficial musings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Threadwrought</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987504#post987504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I'd love to learn more about the Drachid. Like if there was any trouble at first with the first three types of Dragon Kings' Drachid forms interacting (since dinosaurs, pterosaurs, and marine reptiles really were so distinct).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dragon Kings reign lasts at least a hundred million years. We had to gloss over the entire history with incredibly broad strokes. I think it's fair to say that there was likely a period of inter-species conflict before everyone concluded that the Drachid were a unifying force and the Dragon Kings were considered to be one race.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=986986#post986986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ideas on how to involve Rokea?</div> </div> </div> </div>During the actual Dragon wars? Apart from fighting for territory in their own, scrappy, low tech ways, I'd say the Rokea would be prime placed as mercenaries and shock troops - especially if they were equipped with and trained to use specific Mnetic tech and pointed towards pleisiosaur territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987031#post987031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">does it go against the spirit of things, for someone to claim a power for their archid form to let them to explore one of the other breeds turfs? <br /> <br /> e.g. a dino saur becoming airborn, or a pteordectyle deciding to go aquatic, or is that probaly understandable since the setting lets you &amp;quot;Reshape&amp;quot; your archid form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not against the spirit of things at all. The Drachid began the unity of the Kings into one race, the Mnesis and reshaping gave them power to shape their destinies and bodies to reflect who they were on the inside.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987616#post987616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After sending the final draft to the printers, did you fellas ever think &amp;quot;Gee, this has potential to be a Whole Role Playing Game Setting/Rulebook of its own, called &amp;quot;Dreams of The Dragon kings&amp;quot; perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thought about that when I was writing the outline. I'd love the setting to be explored some day.<br /> <br /> But it's ultimately not my choice. White Wolf and Onyx Path shape the view on where they want the story to go, and what will be written and published. If you want more of this, my advice is to vote with your wallets and let Rich know what you love. No guarantees, but it's a start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987739#post987739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ideas on how things would be culinary wise? would they cook their food , is their anything amongst the plants they could use for fermentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>What nikink said. Just thinking out loud here, I'd suggest they probably wouldn't cook food, but would have various Mnetic-derived ways of processing food to preserve it and enhance flavour. This is just one aspect of the setting I'd love to explore if we got the chance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=987739#post987739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It says a Dragon Kings Auspice can change, is it safe to say that their should be a rite for doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>To my mind, there would be a rite akin to some kind of graduation as they move upwards with responsibilities and power. This is one reason why Blazonry was included as a DK-era skill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Threadwrought</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=988014#post988014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you guys considered pitching a Dragon Kings Era book to Onyx Path? Especially once copies of Shattered Dreams are up for everyone to get a look at?</div> </div> </div> </div>See above. We'd love the chance. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Threadwrought</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=988014#post988014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's such a huge era with so much potential. Plus the chance to look at the Insect Wars, perhaps the other early shifters Rokea claim they fought in the depths, the specific varna and breed species that pterosaur, marine reptile, and dinosaur shifters had before the age of Drachid and Dragon Kings, and even the various possibilities for what the Wonder-Work was. There might even be a chance to examine how the earliest proto-Corax and Nagah first started to split away from the Mokole.</div> </div> </div> </div>All great ideas! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:04:58-07:00","id":989526,"title":"","content":"oh on Page 152, is &quot;gracile&quot; supposed to be graceful?<br /> <br /> Hmmmn am I the only one who thinks working resources, 1-5, would help to add flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:45:05-07:00","id":989546,"title":"","content":"Bunyip: I haven't read Shattered Dreams yet, but I plan to get it the day it comes out on DTRPG. My original theory was that the Lunar Exalted created the Changing Breeds, but from what I hear of Shattered Dreams, the Changing Breeds were around a long time before the Exalted era. There is a race of beings called Dragon Kings in Exalted. Any idea what to do with them? Take care. :-)<br /> <br /> <br /> Colleen","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:12:30-07:00","id":989598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=989526#post989526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh on Page 152, is &amp;quot;gracile&amp;quot; supposed to be graceful?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, it's meant to be gracile. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T16:58:34-07:00","id":989619,"title":"","content":"&quot;By the next morning, nothing remains of Shining-Waters except blood-dimmed tides&quot;....I see what ya did there!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T19:47:03-07:00","id":989675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=989546#post989546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bunyip: I haven't read Shattered Dreams yet, but I plan to get it the day it comes out on DTRPG. My original theory was that the Lunar Exalted created the Changing Breeds, but from what I hear of Shattered Dreams, the Changing Breeds were around a long time before the Exalted era. There is a race of beings called Dragon Kings in Exalted. Any idea what to do with them? Take care. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the difficulty is that Exalted and WoD are basically separate. Even if you marry the two as Exalted was a precursor to WoD (which I assume is what you're doing), *something* unimaginably big, cataclysmic, and unknown happened to turn flat-earth Exalted with magical demi-gods into round-world WoD filled with monsters. However you solve that (and whether the two times are continuous or have a separation in between) is the answer to your question.<br /> <br /> But if you want a random thought thrown out there, the whatever-it-was cataclysm that destroyed the Age of Sorrows wiped out everything except Gaia, and it mortally wounded her. Over untold, impossible years, she curled in on herself, hiding her wounds as best she could, slowing her inevitable death but never halting it. In her dying state, she dreams. She dreams on time frame unimaginable to every lesser creature, but as she dreams she has recreated weak shadows of what was, and reimagined the things she knew as the smaller, monstrous forms that inhabit the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T19:52:17-07:00","id":989677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=989675#post989675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the difficulty is that Exalted and WoD are basically separate. Even if you marry the two as Exalted was a precursor to WoD (which I assume is what you're doing), *something* unimaginably big, cataclysmic, and unknown happened to turn flat-earth Exalted with magical demi-gods into round-world WoD filled with monsters. However you solve that (and whether the two times are continuous or have a separation in between) is the answer to your question.<br /> <br /> But if you want a random thought thrown out there, the whatever-it-was cataclysm that destroyed the Age of Sorrows wiped out everything except Gaia, and it mortally wounded her. Over untold, impossible years, she curled in on herself, hiding her wounds as best she could, slowing her inevitable death but never halting it. In her dying state, she dreams. She dreams on time frame unimaginable to every lesser creature, but as she dreams she has recreated weak shadows of what was, and reimagined the things she knew as the smaller, monstrous forms that inhabit the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>yep, for good or ill the whole &quot;Exalted as the prehistory of CWOD&quot; thing has been axed in X20","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T21:00:53-07:00","id":989706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=989619#post989619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;By the next morning, nothing remains of Shining-Waters except blood-dimmed tides&amp;quot;....I see what ya did there