Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You should've seen the ones he made me take out! The section about El-Khaataar's siege on the revolting Drachid *may* have originally been titled &quot;The Empire Strikes Back&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see why that might cause difficulties. I do like the references that appear in books though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T03:42:49-07:00","id":989816,"title":"","content":"So I have to see if your childhood was as fulfilling as mine... <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dino-Riders\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dino-Riders\" target=\"_blank\"> Dino-Riders - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dino-Riders\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dino-Riders </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Inspiration at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T05:34:12-07:00","id":989833,"title":"","content":"I like it. Thank you, Bunyip!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:16:34-07:00","id":990207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=989816#post989816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have to see if your childhood was as fulfilling as mine...<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dino-Riders\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dino-Riders\" target=\"_blank\"> Dino-Riders - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dino-Riders\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dino-Riders </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Inspiration at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's just say, <a href=\"http://static.srcdn.com/wp-content/uploads/dino-riders-movie-mattel.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://static.srcdn.com/wp-content/u...vie-mattel.jpg</a> was my wallpaper for a rather long time... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:48:32-07:00","id":990216,"title":"","content":"I'm going to play the hell out of this setting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:50:44-07:00","id":990219,"title":"","content":"You know, I do have one more question. What would Dragon King language be like? Not just the oral, but the written word? Did they have a system of writing at all that may have come to be before Memetics were widespread? Something similar to Garou Glyphs in a way? <br /> <br /> Also, speaking of past inspirations... Any chance that despite the peaceful nature of it compared to WoD, James Gurney's artwork/writing had a tiny bit of influence? Though this may be a question I should be asking the artists for the chapter, too. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:50:32-07:00","id":990262,"title":"","content":"Ooh, Dinotopia! I haven't thought about that in years! Speaking only for myself - it wasn't an overt inspiration, but I certainly wouldn't rule out bits and pieces of it swirling up out of my subconscious. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As to the inspirations that I'm aware of, for me it was all about the Robert E Howard and the Edgar Rice Burroughs, as well as ancient and Renaissance Mediterranean politics, early Roman Empire military history, and maybe a *dash* of Exalted. For the end of the Empires, I was reading a lot of Jack Vance's Dying Earth and watching Mad Max: Fury Road. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (And of course, seasoned with Dino Riders.)<br /> <br /> Lastly, regarding language - I still really love the idea of no written language, myself, but YMMV. Pictographs make a kind of sense. Spoken language - to me, at any rate - is all about visuals. Visual metaphors, images as cultural touchstones (for those lucky enough to access the Mnesis, that is). <br /> <br /> I'm no linguist, but I could see Drachid language either being very flowery, jamming a lot of detail into every sentence, OR being immensely spartan and practical - when a picture says a thousand words, you don't really need many words, do you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Maybe it's both? Maybe there are whole concepts that the Dragon Kings just *know*, and need very little verbiage around, while the Drachid are left ignorant, with only words to fumble around with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:37:03-07:00","id":990335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=989777#post989777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can see why that might cause difficulties. I do like the references that appear in books though.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it was an EMPIRE! And it was STRIKING BACK! Eh? Eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:48:27-07:00","id":990344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=990335#post990335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it was an EMPIRE! And it was STRIKING BACK! Eh? Eh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes it was and lurking in the shadows of the empire was mezo Mickey just waiting for revenge...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:48:44-07:00","id":990570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=990262#post990262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, Dinotopia! I haven't thought about that in years! Speaking only for myself - it wasn't an overt inspiration, but I certainly wouldn't rule out bits and pieces of it swirling up out of my subconscious. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As to the inspirations that I'm aware of, for me it was all about the Robert E Howard and the Edgar Rice Burroughs, as well as ancient and Renaissance Mediterranean politics, early Roman Empire military history, and maybe a *dash* of Exalted. For the end of the Empires, I was reading a lot of Jack Vance's Dying Earth and watching Mad Max: Fury Road. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (And of course, seasoned with Dino Riders.)<br /> <br /> Lastly, regarding language - I still really love the idea of no written language, myself, but YMMV. Pictographs make a kind of sense. Spoken language - to me, at any rate - is all about visuals. Visual metaphors, images as cultural touchstones (for those lucky enough to access the Mnesis, that is). <br /> <br /> I'm no linguist, but I could see Drachid language either being very flowery, jamming a lot of detail into every sentence, OR being immensely spartan and practical - when a picture says a thousand words, you don't really need many words, do you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Maybe it's both? Maybe there are whole concepts that the Dragon Kings just *know*, and need very little verbiage around, while the Drachid are left ignorant, with only words to fumble around with?</div> </div> </div> </div>That last bit especially strikes a creative chord. Because just imagine you've lived in this society that has lasted for as long as anyone can remember. The language in essence, is pictures and three dimensional shapes your Lords have carried from the Mnesis, as well as their own mixture of body language or pheromones from their saurian side. Even their magnificent Archid forms are a visual message. A display of color, pattern, and texture. Everything comes from your Kings, your rulers, even your own race. <br /> <br /> And then it all changes. Everything is destroyed. You've lost all records, all art, the very root of lasting messages. All in the blink of an eye. It's even worse than a natural disaster, as it permeates -everything-. Wherever imagination was plied, there is now only loss. <br /> <br /> How long would it take the world to recover? The fall of Rome resulted in the Dark Ages, and that was with surviving artifacts and cities. What would happen on a global scale? That would be interesting to tinker with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T13:45:16-07:00","id":990605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Threadwrought</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=990570#post990570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That last bit especially strikes a creative chord. Because just imagine you've lived in this society that has lasted for as long as anyone can remember. The language in essence, is pictures and three dimensional shapes your Lords have carried from the Mnesis, as well as their own mixture of body language or pheromones from their saurian side. Even their magnificent Archid forms are a visual message. A display of color, pattern, and texture. Everything comes from your Kings, your rulers, even your own race. <br /> <br /> And then it all changes. Everything is destroyed. You've lost all records, all art, the very root of lasting messages. All in the blink of an eye. It's even worse than a natural disaster, as it permeates -everything-. Wherever imagination was plied, there is now only loss. <br /> <br /> How long would it take the world to recover? The fall of Rome resulted in the Dark Ages, and that was with surviving artifacts and cities. What would happen on a global scale? That would be interesting to tinker with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice, Threadwrought! Exactly my kind of thinking! <br /> <br /> Actually, I forgot to mention one more inspiration - Mr Robot! Surprising? Well, not if you think about the Mnesis as a kind of magical internet. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T14:45:23-07:00","id":990643,"title":"","content":"Also, I'll guiltily admit... If you guys get the go ahead to do a Mezoic book, I'm also going to be excited to see the art of all the Saurid, Archid, and Drachid forms. &gt;__&gt;<br /> <br /> Also, most of this post apparently disappeared into the ether upon me posting it. O.o<br /> <br /> But just can't wait to see all the options that could be created for not only Mokole, but also Rokea and Ananasi. Just imagine all those prehistoric sharks and the open room to create new, bizarre spiders. <br /> <br /> You even have room for new dinosaurs, or groups within each type of Dragon King corresponding to different saurian groups. From Dinosaurs with Ceratopians and Therapods, to Pterosaurs that have both giants and miniatures in their ranks. And the Marine reptiles have plesiosaurs, Tylosaurus, and perhaps even ancient marine crocodiles. Just... So much possibility!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","user":"Threadwrought","date":".  The ether ate a chunk of my energy drink fueled post. 10-20-2016, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T18:43:49-07:00","id":990740,"title":"","content":"I was absolutely pumped when I got to see the art, too! It's sooooo preeeeeeeetty! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:50:52-07:00","id":991134,"title":"","content":"The Dragon Kings art was amazing and everything I asked for \ud83d\ude00","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T16:44:19-07:00","id":991174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=991134#post991134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dragon Kings art was amazing and everything I asked for \ud83d\ude00</div> </div> </div> </div>BTW, that was your 666th post, Bunyip. I think you need to stop now, or create a new account. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T18:05:45-07:00","id":991633,"title":"","content":"Oh would like to create a gift, as a port of the power of Exalted Dragon Kings &quot;Form of another breed&quot;<br /> <br /> that rank 1, 2, 3, 4, 5?<br /> <br /> I'd say 2, 5 if it doesnt have an activation cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T21:00:56-07:00","id":991696,"title":"","content":"You know, there is one thing I'm curious about. With the Zhong Lung Mokole typically having very different Archid forms from many of their compatriots, and often dreaming of rather different dragon-like creatures rather than just dinosaurs, how would you guys play around with that? Or wold you soften the differences of previous editions? What might the Zhong Lung be dreaming of? <br /> <br /> Is it an undiscovered Saurian, perhaps aquatic, that influences their unusual forms? Or the memory of some line of very stately Dragon Kings with particularly elegant forms? Perhaps even some memory of spirits, Snakes, or an imprint of the Wyrm before it's corruption left in their Mnesis? After all, the Nagah seem to revere the Zhong Lung as connected to the Wani. Perhaps it was from the proto-Zhong that the Snake Varna split from? <br /> <br /> Something else I'm curious about is how were Saurid Dragon Kings treated in a world that increasingly seemed to rely on the Drachid? And moreso, was there any sort of separation or discrimination based on a Dragon King's Saurid line beyond the obvious pterosaur/dinosaur/marine reptile lines? Like... Would there have been any tension or assumptions between a Dragon King with Triceratops ancestry versus one with Deinonychus? And was the Rite for taking new kin developed in the Mezoic so that more Saurian species could be interbred with than those they first developed from?<br /> <br /> Sorry for all the questions again. Just more wandering thoughts. ^_^;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T22:50:27-07:00","id":991736,"title":"","content":"Zhong Lung dreams have been shaped by some 70000 years of living with a cosmology diverging from the cosmologies around other Varna thanks to the Banestorm, and the Wan Xian.<br /> <br /> In the Mesozoic I would think their dreams no different from any others - which means the reverse is also true, with a T Rex Archid form having colourful coils and whiskers as a feasible form for example. I don't think they'd be called the Zhong Lung then, of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Those ancient Mokole who would eventually become ancestors of the Zhong Lung were possibly (and probably, in my head canon) among the most skilled, and most addicted, Wonderworkers - weaving scintillating works of mnesis impossible to tell from reality. By the time what would become known as the Indian Subcontinent collided with what would become known as Asia there were two major factions - those who wove Mnetic illusions and those who rejected them in favour of truly experiencing the realness of Gaia. The Illusionist faction spread east, and their skill with Mnesis, even long after the fall, proved invaluable during the Banestorm, and the rise of the Wan Xian. Then, however, it also became a tool for the Wan Xian to use against them, as they could be fooled and flattered and, crucially, addicted to Mnesis like their long distant ancestors - spending long months in deep introspection.<br /> <br /> YMMV<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:14:09-07:00","id":991891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=991736#post991736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zhong Lung dreams have been shaped by some 70000 years of living with a cosmology diverging from the cosmologies around other Varna thanks to the Banestorm, and the Wan Xian.<br /> <br /> In the Mesozoic I would think their dreams no different from any others - which means the reverse is also true, with a T Rex Archid form having colourful coils and whiskers as a feasible form for example. I don't think they'd be called the Zhong Lung then, of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Those ancient Mokole who would eventually become ancestors of the Zhong Lung were possibly (and probably, in my head canon) among the most skilled, and most addicted, Wonderworkers - weaving scintillating works of mnesis impossible to tell from reality. By the time what would become known as the Indian Subcontinent collided with what would become known as Asia there were two major factions - those who wove Mnetic illusions and those who rejected them in favour of truly experiencing the realness of Gaia. The Illusionist faction spread east, and their skill with Mnesis, even long after the fall, proved invaluable during the Banestorm, and the rise of the Wan Xian. Then, however, it also became a tool for the Wan Xian to use against them, as they could be fooled and flattered and, crucially, addicted to Mnesis like their long distant ancestors - spending long months in deep introspection.<br /> <br /> YMMV<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Mnesis difference is something that I'd thought was best left dropped, along with any kind of punishment for anyone for smacking around the Wan Xian just before they became the Hungry Dead. But then, I have a special chip on my shoulder that came into existence from the latter event as found in Blood and Silk. Had I read said book when it was released and not when it was on sale on DTRPG, I probably would have lost any interest in KotE right then and there, on account of Werewolf's typical pattern of not handing out cosmic punishments when the consequences of no longer having close allies or some manner of resource (hence, Garou and Fera managing to dig their whole deeper) were the end result. Hence, it's this bit of crossover that rankles the worst for me; while just about every other thing that other games say pertaining to Werewolf washes off easily, some part of Werewolf accepted that bit of awkwardness in full.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 10-23-2016, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T11:18:38-07:00","id":991920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=991891#post991891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Mnesis difference is something that I'd thought was best left dropped, along with any kind of punishment for anyone for smacking around the Wan Xian just before they became the Hungry Dead. But then, I have a special chip on my shoulder that came into existence from the latter event as found in Blood and Silk. Had I read said book when it was released and not when it was on sale on DTRPG, I probably would have lost any interest in KotE right then and there, on account of Werewolf's typical pattern of not handing out cosmic punishments when the consequences of no longer having close allies or some manner of resource (hence, Garou and Fera managing to dig their whole deeper) were the end result. Hence, it's this bit of crossover that rankles the worst for me; while just about every other thing that other games say pertaining to Werewolf washes off easily, some part of Werewolf accepted that bit of awkwardness in full.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I haven't read Blood and Silk, what do you mean with this post? I'm just curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:59:02-07:00","id":991998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=991736#post991736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the Mesozoic I would think their dreams no different from any others - which means the reverse is also true, with a T Rex Archid form having colourful coils and whiskers as a feasible form for example. I don't think they'd be called the Zhong Lung then, of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Now, do you mean Archid or Saurid form for the T-Rex form? <br /> <br /> That was one thing in the Dragon Kings chapter that is about my only critique. In a few places it seemed as if Saurid and Archid as terms were mixed up. But, that was the only things I saw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","user":"Threadwrought","date":". 10-23-2016, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:47:53-07:00","id":992104,"title":"","content":"Heh - Saurid, but, mebbe both? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:37:37-07:00","id":992151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=991920#post991920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I haven't read Blood and Silk, what do you mean with this post? I'm just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's where they described the end of the Wan Xian in greater detail, with the aforementioned immortals basically as the Yellow Emperor and associates, with the Beast Courts as Chiyou and allied tribes, right down to Chiyou being, for whatever reason, Hakken. Setting the matter of what Fera he should have been aside for a moment, it described Chiyou as having violated the divine mandate protecting the Wan Xian by striking them for their perfidy, and being cursed to be the only changer doomed to Yomi in the manner similar to the Hungry Dead.<br /> <br /> Of course, back then, it could have been dismissed as the kind of BS claim one game line makes about another. Werewolf was quick to ignore just about everything that other games said about it, so seeing it supported as the way things were in Shattered Dreams was a bit of a shock, even beyond the decision to make the main plot of Dreams a time travel adventure (I never do well with those). Especially since, even if it had to go along with it, it could have at least made Chiyou an Apis, because he was often described as ox-headed. Or perhaps not even involving the fight between Huang Di and Chiyou as a framing reference for the fight, because the details and battle lines just don't fit, even if you twist the story here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:48:35-07:00","id":992158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Threadwrought</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/980415-war-of-the-dragon-kings-discussion?p=991998#post991998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, do you mean Archid or Saurid form for the T-Rex form? <br /> <br /> That was one thing in the Dragon Kings chapter that is about my only critique. In a few places it seemed as if Saurid and Archid as terms wer